Unfolded – Level 3 build prompt for Lovable
Paste everything below the line into the same Lovable project that has Levels 1 and 2. It adds the snake, a second crease choice, a few new puzzle pieces, Level 3 "True Shape" (three rooms), the ending, and a simple star system for replayability. Levels 1 and 2 must keep working exactly as they do now.
Goal
Extend Unfolded with Level 3, "True Shape", the hard tier and the finale. Level 1 taught each mechanic alone. Level 2 added steps, the sword, and the bat. Level 3 makes the mechanics interact (a fold changes the wind, a seal holds a fold, a form change is forced in the middle of a fight) and puts two enemy types in the same space as the puzzle. Priority order: fair and readable challenge, puzzles that need planning, game feel, then polish.
Rules for working in the existing project
• Keep Phaser 3, the same folder structure, constants.ts for every number, and the same data-driven approach: the level is a data file src/game/levels/level3.ts built by the same loader as Levels 1 and 2.
• Reuse existing components (Switch, FoldPlatform, FoldWall, Fan, Slit, Seal, Checkpoint, PromptTag, ExitDoor, the Enemy base class, Bat) and add new ones the same way. Don't rewrite old code unless something has to change; if it does, tell me what and why.
• No image or audio files. All art is drawn in code, all sound is Web Audio.
• Level 3 appears automatically in the main menu and pause menu Room select, grouped under Level 3 with rooms 3A, 3B and 3C.
• The tutorial principles still apply to the hints: short tags, shown only where needed, and never a text wall. Hard means the puzzle needs thinking, not that the controls are unclear.
