• Notice range: 9 tiles horizontally and 3 tiles vertically.
• Reappear position: a valid floor tile (including an unfolded bridge) 3 to 4 tiles from the player, preferably on the side the player is not facing, never on a trap tile or inside a slit.
• Health: 2. The first sword hit staggers it for 0.4 s (flash, knockback 120 px/s) and it vanishes right after, hurt (limp animation, drawn slightly darker). The second hit kills it with a bigger triangle burst and a crunch.
• Damage: 1 hit if the player touches its body or head. Venom does 1 hit.
• Fairness rules: it always shows the Rear telegraph and the Mark before it attacks. It ignores a player who is flat inside a slit. It cannot spit while the player is flat inside a slit. It never appears on top of the player. The snake does not coil around the player.
• Respawn: after dying, it respawns after 25 s at its patrol start, but only if the room has not been cleared. A room counts as cleared once the player has passed its exit for the first time.
• Sounds: hiss (band-passed noise), a soft crumple when it vanishes, a pop when it appears, a wet spit.
Venom
• A dark magenta #8E2D6B triangle blob that rotates as it flies.
• Launched at 300 px/s toward where the player was at the end of the Aim state, with gravity 600 px/s² so it travels in an arc. It does not track.
• Destroyed on hitting a solid or the player. Damage 1.
• Wind: inside a fan's draught venom gets +900 px/s² upward, so a gust bends the arc.
• With the Parry crease, a slash that overlaps the venom reflects it at 1.3× speed toward the snake, and the snake takes 1 damage from it.
New puzzle pieces
Timed Switch. Works like Switch, but stays pressed for 7 seconds after the player steps on it, then releases. A ring around the plate empties as the time runs out, and the dotted link line to its targets fades in step with it. Reuse the switch art but draw it with a small clock-like ring.
Fold Sheet. A thin horizontal purple sheet (4 px thick, solid). While closed it blocks a fan's draught: the fan's column is cut off just below any solid above the fan. When its trigger fires (a switch or a released seal) it folds away to the side over 0.4 s, and the column reaches its full height. A sheet never closes while the player or an enemy overlaps it; it waits until the space is clear.
Fold Bridge. A platform made of 5 segments of 2 tiles each, starting folded (dashed ghost, no collision). On unfolding, the segments open one after another 0.1 s apart from left to right like a concertina, each swinging out around its crease with angle shading and a small dust burst. Collision turns on per segment when it lands.
Seal links. A seal can hold another object closed (heldBy). Draw a thin teal thread from the seal to the object it holds. Cutting the seal releases the object, snaps the thread, and plays a twang.
Second crease choice
After the Level 2 exit door, and before Level 3 starts, show the "Choose a crease" screen again, now with two new cards. The choice is added to the first one (the player keeps both). If Level 3 is started from the menu without having made this choice, show the screen first.
Crease
Effect
Quick fold
The player can enter flat form in mid-air, and moves at 280 px/s (instead of 200) while flat. It makes slits faster and safer to use.
Parry crease
A slash that overlaps a venom blob reflects it at 1.3× speed and it damages the snake.
No room requires a crease. Parry gives one alternative way to beat the snake without melee. Quick fold is a comfort upgrade and does not create a shortcut. Show the earned creases as small icons under the health.
Visual style for Level 3
