Level 3 layout
World is 120 tiles wide and 24 tall. The main floor surface is at row 20 (y = 640 px). h means tiles above the main floor. The camera follows vertically with a gentle lerp and the same deadzone as before. Every room has a checkpoint at its entrance.
Room 3A: Fold, wind and the bat (x 0 to 36)
Goal of the room: the way up is blocked by a sheet that only a distant switch can open, and the switch is timed.
• Floor h=0 from x 0 to 36, closed by a wall at x 0 on the left. Checkpoint at x 1.
• Fan at x 6–7 on the floor. Its column (2 wide, 10 tiles tall) is cut off by the sheet below.
• Fold Sheet at h=5, x 4–9 (6 wide), above the fan.
• Overhang ledge, a 1-tile-thick slab from x 12 to 36 with its top at h=8 (256 px). The floor is open underneath. It can't be reached by jumping.
• Timed Switch on the floor at x 22, under the overhang. Target: the sheet. Duration 7 s.
• Bat hanging from a ceiling strip at x 8–11, anchor at h=12, above the landing area. It alerts as the player rises.
• Solution: step on the timed switch, run back to the fan (about 15 tiles) before the 7 s run out, ride the draught up past the bat, and drift right onto the ledge (4 tiles from the column's edge). Walk along the ledge to the next room.
• Why it's Hard: a timed action far from the place where it pays off, wind that only works after a fold, and a bat in the draught that bends its dive. The sheet waits if the player is still in it when the timer ends, so nobody gets crushed.
Room 3B: Slit, seal, bridge and the snake (x 36 to 76)
Goal of the room: open the way across a gap while a snake guards the far side.
• This room is a raised block with its floor at h=8 from x 36 to 76. Checkpoint at x 37.
• Slit pillar at x 40–46 (6 tiles long, 7 tiles tall, 14 px clearance).
• Calm arena from x 46 to 52, no enemies.
• Seal at x 52, from h=8 up to h=16 under a ceiling block, so it can't be jumped over. A teal thread runs from it to the Fold Bridge.
• Gap from x 56 to 66 (10 tiles), with the pit floor at h=6 (2 tiles down, safe, and the player can jump out of it).
• Fold Bridge over the gap, top at h=8, 5 segments, held closed by the seal.
• Snake with home at x 70 and patrol from x 67 to 75, on the far side.
• The floor continues to x 76, the exit of the room.
• Solution: slide through the slit, unfold in the calm arena, draw the sword and cut the seal, which releases the bridge, then cross the bridge while the snake teleports and spits, and defeat or avoid it.
• Why it's Hard: form change, then the sword, then a forced crossing under fire. The snake can reappear on the bridge itself, and a hit knocks the player toward the pit (safe), so a mistake costs time, not the whole room.
• Parry alternative: reflect the snake's own venom to kill it from a distance.
Room 3C: All three mechanics and both enemies (x 76 to 120)
Goal of the room: the finale. Drop into a shaft, get past a slit and a snake, cut a seal, and use the freed draught to reach the exit under a bat.
• Entry ledge at x 76–86 with its top at h=8. Checkpoint at x 77. The ledge ends in a drop of 8 tiles (safe) into the shaft, which has its floor at h=0 from x 86 to 120. A second checkpoint on the landing at x 87, so a reset doesn't send the player back through room 3B.
• Slit pillar at x 90–93 (3 tiles long, 7 tiles tall, 14 px clearance), right after the landing.
• Snake arena from x 93 to 99. The snake's home is x 96, patrol x 94–98. It ignores the player while they are flat inside the slit, and starts to Rear as they come out.
• Seal at x 99, from h=0 to h=6 under a ceiling block. A teal thread runs up to the Fold Sheet.
• Fold Sheet at h=9, x 100–106, above the fan, held closed by the seal.
• Fan at x 102–103. Its column is 16 tiles tall (to h=16), cut off by the sheet until the seal is cut.
• High platform at x 108–120 with its top at h=14 (448 px), with the exit door at x 118.
• Bat hanging from a ceiling strip at x 104–107, anchor at h=18, above the platform's edge. It alerts as the player rises in the draught, and its dive bends in the column.
• Solution: drop in, slide through the slit, unfold, deal with the snake (kill it, or dodge its attacks and break its rhythm), draw the sword and cut the seal, which releases the sheet, run to the fan, ride up past the bat, and drift right onto the platform.
• Why it's Hard: every mechanic and both enemies in one connected sequence, where the player must decide when to fight and when to move.
