Difficulty rules to keep
• Each Hard room needs 3 or more steps and at least two mechanics affecting each other.
• Every attack has a telegraph, and no attack lands on a player who could not see it coming.
• A failed attempt costs time, never the whole level: shallow pits, checkpoints at every room entrance, and one extra checkpoint after the 3C drop.
• Nothing is required from a crease.
Hints
Short paper tags only: in 3A "The switch is timed" near the switch and "The sheet blocks the wind" near the fan, in 3B "Cut it" at the seal, "Watch the crease" the first time a snake Mark appears, and, if the player has Parry, "Slash the venom" the first time venom flies. After 3 failures at the same spot its tag reappears with a gentle pulse. Never solve it for the player.
The ending
Walking into the 3C exit door starts a short sequence of about 12 seconds, all drawn in code:
1.  The player stops and the paper pieces that make the figure drift apart and float.
2.  The pieces unfold one by one into a single flat, blank paper square, which is the character's true shape. Soft chime notes rise as each piece lands.
3.  The camera pulls back to show the three levels as a pattern of creases on that same sheet.
4.  The title "Unfolded" fades in.
5.  Then the Game complete screen: total time, total resets, total hits taken, the creases chosen, and a line suggesting to replay with the other creases. Buttons: Play again, Main menu.
The player must be able to skip it with Enter after the first 2 seconds.
